From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:53:04 +0000
Subject: fix: allow WebContentsImpl::CenterSelection on all platforms

WebContentsImpl::CenterSelection() wraps its whole body in
BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC), so it does nothing on Windows and Linux. The guard
was copied from the neighbouring CopyToFindPboard() when
CenterSelection was added in https://crrev.com/c/4258445, but only
CopyToFindPboard needs it, because only macOS has a find pasteboard.
The rest of the path is platform-neutral: the
FrameWidgetInputHandler.CenterSelection mojom message,
FrameWidgetInputHandlerImpl, WebFrameWidgetImpl and
WebLocalFrameImpl::CenterSelection(), which calls RevealSelection()
with ScrollAlignment::CenterAlways().

Removing the guard makes Electron's webContents.centerSelection() and
<webview>.centerSelection() work on Windows and Linux.

This should be upstreamed. Drop this patch once upstream
WebContentsImpl::CenterSelection() is no longer guarded by
BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC).

diff --git a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
index c5cb7939d67bf9189643773d3e24f937aaec8b14..5270bcbdda400512086941758ba7554b683967b6 100644
--- a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
@@ -7272,7 +7272,6 @@ void WebContentsImpl::CopyToFindPboard() {
 
 void WebContentsImpl::CenterSelection() {
   OPTIONAL_TRACE_EVENT0("content", "WebContentsImpl::CenterSelection");
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
   auto* input_handler = GetFocusedFrameWidgetInputHandler();
   if (!input_handler) {
     return;
@@ -7280,7 +7279,6 @@ void WebContentsImpl::CenterSelection() {
 
   last_interaction_time_ = ui::EventTimeForNow();
   input_handler->CenterSelection();
-#endif
 }
 
 void WebContentsImpl::Paste() {
